  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Equality Now Nairobi/SOAWR Coalition - All for Maputo Protocol Initiative</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Equality Now Nairobi/SOAWR Coalition - All for Maputo Protocol Initiative</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Long term goal
The rights of women and girls under the Maputo Protocol are promoted and protected and any violations are remedied.

Mid-term outcomes
* At least 2-6 countries targeted by the Maputo Protocol have ratified the Maputo protocol.
* Greater domestication of the Maputo Protocol by 8-10 countries that have ratified.
* Greater accountability by at least 8-10 countries that have ratified the Maputo Protocol

Short term goals (what is expected to be different at the end of the project period)
* Stronger, committed and results-oriented SOAWR Coalition implementing the All for Maputo Protocol Initiative.
* Greater public awareness and pressure on governments to ratify, domesticate and implement the Maputo Protocol in 6-8 countries.
* Governments of 6-8 countries recognize the importance of ratification, domestication and implementation of the Maputo Protocol.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Recognizing the persistent gender inequality and discriminatory practices against women in Africa, the AU Assembly adopted the Protocol to the African Charter on Human and Peoples Rights on the Rights of Women in Africa 2003 in Maputo, Mozambique. The Maputo Protocol remains one of the most comprehensive and progressive instruments on women&#x2019;s and girls&#x2019; rights with most of its provisions being tailored to the realities of the African continent. However, universal ratification has not been achieved and the domestication and implementation of the Protocol is at best poor. 

To amplify the progress, AU launched the All for Maputo Protocol Programme (AMPP) last year (2018) with the objective of universal ratification, domestication and implementation of the Maputo Protocol by all Member States accompanied by enforcement mechanisms involving the African Court on Human and Peoples&#x2019; Rights and the AU Special Rapporteur on Women&#x2019;s Rights. The Solidarity for African Women&#x2019;s Rights (SOAWR) Coalition, working closely with the AU Women Gender and Development Directorate (WGDD), was involved in the development and design of the AMPP and has been recognized as a key strategic partner in the implementation of the programme.

Sida will contribute with funding of 20 MSEK during 2019-2023 for a project that will support the SOAWR Coalition&#x2019;s contribution to the achievements of the AMPP and goes under the name &#x201c;All for Maputo Protocol Initiative&#x201d;. The project/Initiative is expected to result in;
&#x2022;	A stronger coalition of women&#x2019;s rights organizations engaged in joint action to ensure the implementation of the All for Maputo Protocol Initiative. 
&#x2022;	An approved and adopted 5-year Strategic Plan to guide the SOAWR Coalition. 
&#x2022;	A stronger push by CSO actors for the ratification of the Maputo Protocol by the remaining 14 countries to achieve universal ratification.
&#x2022;	Improved domestication of the Protocol through national laws, policies and jurisprudence, and implementation.
&#x2022;	An informed citizenry that is able to claim the rights of women and girls and are able to hold their governments to account on their obligations under the Protocol.
&#x2022;	Greater engagement of different classes of citizens with the Protocol at the national, regional and continental levels &#x2013; specially targeting the youth, media, creatives, academia and leaders/influencers.
&#x2022;	Increased quality reporting to the African Commission within the set guidelines by Member States and CSOs.

Sida will enter into agreement with Equality Now Nairobi, convening the SOAWR Coalition in its function as Secretariat.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Som ett erk&#xe4;nnande av den best&#xe4;ndiga oj&#xe4;mlikheten och fortsatta diskrimineringen av kvinnor i Afrika s&#xe5; antog den Afrikanska Unionen (AU) ett protokoll till den afrikanska stadgan om m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter och folkets r&#xe4;ttigheter 2003 i Maputo med fokus p&#xe5; kvinnors r&#xe4;ttigheter. D&#xe4;refter kallat Maputoprotokollet. Maputoprotokollet &#xe4;r fortsatt en av de mer omfattande och progressiva instrumenten f&#xf6;r att driva kampen f&#xf6;r kvinnor och flickors r&#xe4;ttigheter, med ett inneh&#xe5;ll som &#xe4;r regionalt f&#xf6;rankrat. Trots detta har universell ratificering inte uppn&#xe5;tts och till&#xe4;mningen av protokollets inneh&#xe5;ll &#xe4;r som b&#xe4;st begr&#xe4;nsad. 

F&#xf6;r att driva p&#xe5; utvecklingen lanserade AU programmet All for Maputo Protocol Programme (AMPP) f&#xf6;rra &#xe5;ret (2018) med syftet att n&#xe5; universell ratificering och fullst&#xe4;ndig till&#xe4;mpning av protokollets samtliga artiklar. Koalitionen Solidarity for African Women&#x2019;s Rights (SOAWR), en samlingsorganisation f&#xf6;r kvinnor&#xe4;ttsorganisationer som arbetar f&#xf6;r genomf&#xf6;randet av Maputoprotokollet, har varit instrumentell i framtagandet och utformningen av AMPP tillsammans med AUs Women Gender and Development Directorate (WGDD), och har erk&#xe4;nts som en strategisk partner i genomf&#xf6;randet av programmet. 

Sida kommer att bidra med 20 miljoner svenska kronor i finansiering under perioden 2019-2023 till ett projekt som kommer att m&#xf6;jligg&#xf6;ra SOAWRs bidrag till genomf&#xf6;randet av AMPP. Projektet ben&#xe4;mns som &#x201c;The All for Maputo Protocol Initiative&#x201d; och f&#xf6;rv&#xe4;ntas resultera i f&#xf6;ljande:
-En starkare koalition/samarbetsplattform av kvinnor&#xe4;ttsorganisationer som &#xe4;r engagerade i gemensamt arbete och genomf&#xf6;randet av projektet All for Maputo Protocol Initiative.
-En godk&#xe4;nd och antagen 5-&#xe5;rig strategisk plan som styr koalitionens arbete. 
-Ett starkare tryck fr&#xe5;n civilsamh&#xe4;llesakt&#xf6;rer f&#xf6;r att de 14 l&#xe4;nder som &#xe4;nnu inte har ratificerat Maputoprotokollet g&#xf6;r det. 
-Att fler l&#xe4;nder har anpassat nationella juridiska system i enlighet med Maputoprotokollets inneh&#xe5;ll.
-En b&#xe4;ttre informerad allm&#xe4;nhet som har m&#xf6;jlighet att kr&#xe4;va r&#xe4;ttigheter f&#xf6;r kvinnor och flickor, samt har m&#xf6;jlighet att h&#xe5;lla sina regeringar ansvariga f&#xf6;r att leva upp till Maputoprotokollet.
-&#xd6;kat deltagande och engagemang f&#xf6;r Maputoprotokollet p&#xe5; nationell, regional och kontinental niv&#xe5; &#x2013; med s&#xe4;rskilt fokus p&#xe5; unga, media, personer med kreativa yrken, akademin och personer i ledande position/influencers.  
-&#xd6;kad kvalitativ rapportering p&#xe5; efterlevnaden av Maputoprotokollet till den Afrikanska kommissionen enligt de riktlinjer som best&#xe4;mts av medlemsstater och civilsamh&#xe4;llet.  

Sida kommer att sluta avtal med Equality Now Nairobi som sammankallar SOAWR genom sin roll som koalitionens sekretariat.</narrative>
  </description>
